details:
(a) whether Government has conducted any national study on the time lag between the issuance of lightning warnings and the dissemination of such information to the last person in remote villages;
(b) whether an automated warning system based on sirens, community radio and village-level equipments are being developed for areas lacking mobile network connectivity; and
(c) whether there is any proposal to launch a pilot project of a ‘Last-Mile Lightning Warning Grid’ in Jharkhand?

(a) whether there is any national system in place to record a separate health history of long-term exposure to dust, contaminated water and industrial pollution in the health examinations of citizens living in mining areas;
(b) whether there is a proposal to develop a digital 'Environmental Exposure Health Record' for such areas and link it with the primary health system; and
(c) whether its pilot implementation will be initiated for children, women and communities living around mines in the mining-affected districts of Jharkhand?

(a) whether the State-wise number of families deprived of reliable electricity in remote forest and tribal villages solely due to waiting for the extension of the main electricity grid has been assessed;
(b) whether there is a proposal to develop a solar, battery, and local micro-grid-based ‘Energy Access Guarantee Model’ for such villages; and
(c) whether a pilot implementation of this model will be undertaken to provide 24-hour essential electricity in the inaccessible forest villages of Jharkhand?

(a) whether there has been any national mapping of the quantity, quality and potable and irrigation usability of water accumulated in the country's closed and abandoned mines;
(b) whether there is a proposal to develop a mine water resource grid for the use of such water after scientific treatment; and
(c) whether a pilot project will be initiated to link the water from abandoned mines in the State of Jharkhand's water-scarce mining areas to rural drinking water and irrigation systems?

(a) whether there is any national mechanism to assess the employment, local trade, and revenue dependence of the respective district five or ten years prior to the closure of coal mines; 
(b) whether there is a proposal to make a mandatory 'Pre-Closure District Economic Transition Plan for each coal-dependent district; and 
(c) whether such a plan would be implemented as a pilot project in the coal-rich districts of Jharkhand for alternative industries, skill development, and local employment generation before the closure of mines?

(a) whether Government has conducted any assessment of available passenger rail services vis-a-vis freight transportation in the coal and mineral-producing regions of Jharkhand;
(b) if so, the details of new passenger rail services introduced, new trains sanctioned and pending proposals in Jharkhand over the last five years; and
(c) whether Government is considering introducing new rail services or expanding existing ones in Jharkhand keeping in view the needs of passengers in mining and industrial areas?

(a) whether Government has conducted any evaluation of central assistance being provided to universities, research institutes and startup ecosystems in Jharkhand for science and technology-based research; 
(b) if so, the details of research projects, innovation programmes and financial assistance approved in the State during the last five years; and 
(c) whether Government is considering to initiate any special science and technology programme in the State, in order to promote research related to mining, tribal livelihoods, agriculture, water conservation and clean energy?

(a) whether Government has assessed complaints regarding card-holding beneficiaries being denied treatment, hospitals refusing to accept cards, and pending claims under the Ayushman Bharat Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY) across various States of the country;
(b) if so, the details regarding complaints received from the States, the action taken thereon, and the hospital-wise details thereof during the last five years; and
(c) whether Government is considering developing an effective monitoring and accountability mechanism to ensure timely and prompt treatment for eligible beneficiaries?

(a) whether the Central Government has undertaken any district-wise assessment of the status of establishment, financial assistance provided and employment generation with regard to Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) in the State of Jharkhand;
(b) if so, the details of the MSME units registered, loans sanctioned, employment generated and units closed during the last five years; and
(c) whether Government is considering launching any special incentive programme to promote MSMEs based on minerals, Tasar, handicrafts and forest produce in the State of Jharkhand?

(a) whether Government has assessed the progress of the development of mineral-based industries, industrial corridors and export-oriented manufacturing units in Jharkhand;
(b) if so, the details of the industrial projects sanctioned, investment proposals and central assistance provided for export promotion in Jharkhand during the last five years; and
(c) whether Government is considering to implement any special policy or incentive package for the development of value-addition-based industries and export-oriented industrial clusters in Jharkhand?

(a) whether Government has conducted any assessment on the status of conservation and promotion of tribal cultural heritage, archaeological sites and traditional folk arts of Jharkhand;
(b) if so, the details of conservation projects sanctioned, central assistance provided and their current progress in the State during the last five years; and 
(c) whether Government is considering to implement any special action plan to promote the tribal cultural heritage of the State at national and international levels?

(a) whether Government has conducted any assessment of the quality of school education, availability of teachers and that of the status of school infrastructure in the tribal and aspirational districts of Jharkhand;
(b) if so, the district-wise major findings thereof in respect of Jharkhand and the assistance provided by the Central Government for addressing teacher vacancies and strengthening digital education and school infrastructure; and
(c) whether Government is considering any special programme or additional financial assistance to improve access to secondary and higher secondary education in the tribal-majority areas of Jharkhand, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the implementation of schemes related to nutrition, anemia and safety for women and girls in the tribal and aspirational districts of Jharkhand;
(b) if so, the main findings thereof and the amount of Central assistance provided for the said schemes in Jharkhand during the last five years; and
(c) whether Government is considering to implement a special action plan to strengthen nutrition and women's safety programmes in the high-risk tribal areas of Jharkhand?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the implementation of solar, biomass and other decentralized renewable energy projects in tribal and remote areas of Jharkhand;
(b) if so, the details of approved projects, benefited villages and central assistance provided during the last five years; and
(c) whether Government is considering to implement a special programme to expand decentralized clean energy projects in remote areas of Jharkhand where power supply is still erratic?

(a) whether Government has carried out any assessment of the reach, broadcasting quality and availability of programmes in local languages ??by All India Radio and Doordarshan in the tribal and remote areas of Jharkhand;
(b) if so, the key findings thereof and the steps taken during last five years to strengthen broadcasting services in these areas; and
(c) whether Government is considering the expansion of programmes by public broadcasters in order to preserve and promote the tribal languages ??and local culture of Jharkhand?

(a) whether Government has approved any special plan for the modernization, capacity expansion, and adoption of new technology of the Central Public Sector heavy industries and industrial units located in Jharkhand in the last five years; 
(b) if so, the unit-wise details, approved investment, and current progress; and 
(c) Government's assessment regarding the creation of direct and indirect employment for local youth in Jharkhand by means of these plans?

(a) whether Government has conducted any scientific study or independent assessment regarding the health environment and radiation safety impacts on the people residing in and around the uranium mining and processing area of Jharkhand during the last five years;
(b) if so, the major findings thereof and the corrective and precautionary measures taken in Jharkhand on the basis thereof; and
(c) whether Government is implementing any long-term action plan for health monitoring, safe drinking water, environmental surveillance and the welfare of local community in these areas and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the share of total CSR spent by all steel sector units including SAIL, NMDC, MECON and large private companies on mining affected tribal areas of Jharkhand during 2023-24 and 2024-25, the details thereof;
(b) whether it is a fact that many companies spend a large portion of their CSR funds on metropolitan, branding events and other non-essential heads, while basic facilities continue to remain inadequate in villages located around mining areas of Jharkhand and environmental pollution in such areas is becoming increasingly serious; and
(c) whether companies are taking measures to address these issues, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the Central Government has given approval for the construction of 2,22,069 new houses under the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Rural) in Jharkhand for the year 2025-26;
(b) if so, the amount of fund sanctioned by the Central Government to construct these houses, the details thereof; and
(c) whether an assistance amount of ?1.30 lakh per house is being provided in tribal and difficult areas of Jharkhand, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the payment of ?545.97 crore has been made to 19,97,224 farmers of Jharkhand in the 18th installment of PM-KISAN scheme; 
(b) if so, whether this amount is lower than previous installments, the reasons therefor along with the details thereof; and
(c) the number of farmers excluded from PM-KISAN scheme in the State of Jharkhand along with the number of farmers whose payments are stalled due to non-e-KYC, non-seeding of land or due to other reasons, the details thereof?

(a) the steps taken by the Central Government to ensure timely recognition and accreditation of AYUSH educational institutions by the National Commission for Indian System of Medicine (NCISM) and National Commission for Homoeopathy (NCH);
(b) whether delay in approvals is causing difficulties to the students in obtaining admission; and
(c) the reasons for the Central Government’s failure to fill vacancies in key Ayush teaching institutions despite available State-level proposals?

(a) whether the State of Jharkhand owns approximately 27–32 per cent of country’s total coal reserves, if so, the reasons for the headquarters of Coal India not being located in the State of Jharkhand;
(b) the reason for not planing to establish the headquarters of Coal India in the State of Jharkhand despite the fact that it would promote employment, technical expertise, and development in the State; and
(c) whether Government would put an end to the discrimination being faced by the people of the State of Jharkhand and the Centre, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has issued guidelines to ensure adequate health, hygiene and sanitation infrastructure in EMRS hostels, especially for girl students, if so, details thereof;
(b) whether EMRS across various States are equipped with separate and functional toilets, access to menstrual hygiene products;
(c) whether any audit or inspection has been conducted to assess the quality of health and sanitation infrastructure in EMRS hostels over the last three years, if so, details thereof; and
(d) whether any case of dropout or absenteeism has been reported due to inadequate hostel facilities, particularly among female students, if so, the corrective measures taken?

(a) whether Government has taken any step to improve enrolment and retention of students from SC, ST, OBC and minority communities in higher education, particularly in professional and postgraduate courses;
(b) whether Government has conducted any internal evaluation or third-party review to assess the effectiveness of such interventions, if so, its key findings; and
(c) whether any initiative has been taken or any incentives are being provided to improve faculty diversity in centrally funded institutions, particularly for the recruitment and promotion of faculty members from SC, ST, OBC and minority backgrounds, if so, the details thereof?

a) whether Government is aware of the disruptions in the global supply of rare earth magnets due to recent geopolitical developments such as Chinese export restrictions;
b) the present limit of India's current dependency on imported rare earth magnets, particularly the share of rare earth magnets sourced from China along with the total volume imported over the last three financial years;
c) whether Government assessed the potential impact of these supply disruptions on domestic manufacturing of automobile and electric vehicle; and
d) the steps Government has taken to reduce India’s dependence on imported rare earth magnets?

(a) whether Government is aware of US student visa issues being faced by prospective Indian students;
(b) if so, the details thereof; 
(c) whether Government is taking any active steps to solve the issues;
(d) if so, the details of steps taken thereof; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has sanctioned ? 24,104 crores for Pradhan Mantri Janjati Adivasi Nyaya Maha Abhiyan (PM JANMAN) with a Central Share of ? 15,336 crore and State share of ? 8,768 crore;
(b) whether the aim of the awareness programme is to reach out to 22000 Particularly Vulnerable Tribal Groups (PVTGs) majority tribal habitations and PVTG families in 200 districts across the country; and
(c) if so, the details of the measures being taken so far, and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether the FSSAI has set standards for non-bovine (sheep, goat, camel, donkey) milk, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether an Entrepreneurship Development Programme (EDP) has been implemented for sheep, goat, camel and donkey under National Livestock Mission (NLM), if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the subsidy provided to farmers, Farmer Producer Organization (FPO), Farmer Cooperative Organizations (FCO), Self Help Groups (SHG) and Joint Liability Groups (JLG) under this scheme and the manner in which it helps in promotion of livestock products, the State-wise details thereof?

(a) the details of the schemes in place to promote indigenous crafts and skills among minority communities;
(b) the steps taken by Government to help minority artisans access wider markets and fair prices;
(c) whether there are training programs for young artisans to modernize and preserve traditional techniques, if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the steps taken to link minority artisans with tourism, exports or digital platforms?
bs

(a) whether Government has conducted a detailed study on health problems, particularly respiratory and skin diseases, in mining sectors to verify the findings of the survey conducted by National Foundation for India;
(b) the concrete steps taken so far to address the long-term health related problems of coal miners and their families in the States of Jharkhand, Chhattisgarh and Odisha; and
(c) whether Government proposes to set up special health facilities or mobile health units for workers and their families in the affected districts?

(a) whether Government has taken steps to monitor the State-wise distribution of funds especially Bihar, Punjab, Uttarakhand and Chhattisgarh under the 15th Finance Commission Grants, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government has established any mechanism to ensure the equitable distribution of these grants, considering the population size and rural development needs of different States, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether there are any proposed policy adjustments to enhance the efficiency, transparency and impact of fund utilization in future disbursements, if so, the details thereof?

(a) details of progress made, area covered, funds allocated and expenditure incurred under Ganga Bank Tree Plantation Campaign (2016-21) in the State of Jharkhand;
(b) out of ?347 crores, amount allocated to Jharkhand and utilized thereof, the measures taken for efficient use of funds and achievement of goals;
(c) impact of tree plantation on groundwater recharging and preventing erosion in the State;
(d) the steps taken to enhance the success of the campaign and ensure participation of local community for sustainable results; and 
(e) plan to identify the areas of Jharkhand affected by changes in the flow of Ganga and the resolution thereof?

(a) whether Government has formulated a balanced nutrient management scheme under the recommendations of Indian Council of Agricultural Research (ICAR) to prevent the decline in soil quality, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government has implemented a soil health and fertility scheme to assist State Governments in issuing soil health cards to farmers, if so, the details thereof, State-wise; and
(c) the number of soil health cards that have been generated so far and the benefits received by farmers in terms of improved soil quality, the details thereof, State-wise?

(a) the financial assistance given under National Sports Development Fund (NSDF) for sports infrastructure, training and promotion in Jharkhand during the last three years;
(b) the steps taken by Government to promote tribal and traditional games in Jharkhand under NSDF and other schemes;
(c) whether the Sports Authority of India (SAI) Centre in Jharkhand has been upgraded under NSDF, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the number of sports persons from Jharkhand received international coaching, technical assistance or competition participation under NSDF during the last five years?
P

(a) whether Government has prepared a detailed action plan under the Financial Assistance for Promotion of Guru-Shishya Parampara (Repertory Grant) for performing arts activities such as drama groups, theatre groups, music troupes and children's theatre, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the criteria under which the assistance is provided to gurus and shishyas under this scheme, the details thereof;
(c) whether this scheme has encouraged emerging artists in the field of traditional art forms and performing arts, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the State-wise details of number of gurus and shishyas provided financial assistance under this scheme so far?

(a) whether Government has prepared a detailed action plan to provide internship opportunities to one crore youth under the Pradhan Mantri Internship Scheme (PMIS) announced in the Budget 2024-25, the details thereof;
(b) the steps being taken to partner with top 500 companies under this scheme; the details thereof;
(c) whether this scheme would improve the employability skills and future employment opportunities of the youth, the details thereof; and
(d) the details of internships provided under this scheme, State-wise?

(a) the reasons for only 2,713 households in the State of Jharkhand getting tap water in December 2024, whereas the number was higher earlier and the steps taken to reinstate the scheme;
(b) whether rural families in the State of Jharkhand, Rajasthan, and West Bengal are deprived of clean drinking water due to delay on the part of the Central Government and the details of immediate steps taken to address this issue; and
(c) whether Government acknowledges the nine months delay in releasing fund as a hindrance to the supply of drinking water under the Jal Jeevan Mission despite the allocation of ? 2114.22 crore for the same?

(a) whether any special programme has been organized for the folk arts and tribal artists of Jharkhand under Promotion and Preservation of Tribal and Folk Arts scheme;
(b) if so, the details of these programmes and if not, the reasons therefor; and
(c) the number of tribal artists of Jharkhand who have been provided financial assistance under Promotion and Preservation of Tribal and Folk Arts scheme?

(a) whether the Ministry is planning to set up new vocational training centres in the tribal areas of Jharkhand;
(b) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and
(c) the total number of beneficiaries benefited from the vocational training centres currently operating in the tribal areas of Jharkhand?

(a) the progress made in establishing the promised cluster-based lac processing units so far in Jharkhand, aimed at ensuring fair prices to farmers for their produce;
(b) the expected timeline for completion of the establishment of cluster-based lac processing units in Jharkhand, along with the Government’s plan to monitor their performance; and 
(c) the current status of financial allocation and implementation process in Jharkhand for setting up lac processing units?

(a) the plan being formulated under the India Semiconductor Mission (ISM) to control greenhouse gas emissions and water usage in the proposed semiconductor fabs to ensure compliance with India's climate commitments;
(b) the details of the steps to be taken for regulating the use of chemicals and gases, including Fluorinated gases (F-gases) regulations and the ban on Per- and Polyfluoroalkyl Substances (PFASs), in the semiconductor manufacturing process; and 
(c) the details of the monitoring and accountability mechanisms that will be implemented to ensure regular assessment and mitigation of the environmental impact of the semiconductor fab projects?

(a) the steps being taken by Government to improve employment share in the construction sector which was 12.8 per cent in 2012 and declined to 11.4 per cent in 2024 as per Periodic Labour Force Survey (PLFS) report;
(b) the strategy devised to curb the alarming rise in unpaid family labour in agriculture, which has been recorded as employment in the PLFS survey;
(c) the reasons for the lack of growth in the share of employment in the construction sector over the last five years; and
(d) the impact of the Central Government schemes like Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana on unemployment trends in rural areas?

(a) whether, after the opening of Agartala- Akhaura railway project, Government is planning any other economic development project for North Eastern Region;
(b) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor;
(c) whether Government is planning to open any passenger train through Agartala-Akhaura rail route; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has taken any initiatives to preserve the tribal culture in the country;
(b) if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the details of schemes launched in Financial Year 2022-23 and 2023-24 to preserve the culture of tribals?

(a) whether Government has plans to adopt the Public- Private- Partnership model to modernize the health ecosystem of district hospitals in the country as suggested by the NITI-Aayog;
(b) if so, the details thereof; and
(c) if not, whether Government has come up with any other alternative to modernize the healthcare system at the district level in the country?

(a) whether Government has set up a timeline to amend the Information Technology (IT) Rules of 2021 to add new rules to regulate Artificial Intelligence (AI);
(b) if so, the details thereof, if not, the reasons therefor;
(c) whether Government plans to have a specific provision to safeguard user data and ensure transparency in data handling by AI systems under the new rules; and
(d) if so, the details thereof, if not, the reasons therefor?
K

(a) whether Government is creating a special farm sector index for lifting agricultural productivity and incomes in the country;
(b) if so, the details on key components or indicators that will be included in the special farm sector indices;
(c) the manner in which these components are selected, the details thereof;
(d) whether these components are selected to reflect the overall performance of the agricultural sector, if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and
(e) the manner in which the special farm sector indices can address challenges in the agriculture sector through targeted policy interventions?

(a) the state/UT-wise details of the number of beneficiaries of the National Overseas Scholarship for tribal students;
(b) the state/UT-wise details of the funds disbursed to students under the scheme;
(c) the number of awardees for this scholarship for FY23-FY24 from Jharkhand;
(d) whether Government is taking steps to promote awareness regarding this scheme among students from tribal populations in the eastern parts of India; and
(e) if so, the details thereof, and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government is taking effective measures to reduce the transmission rate of HIV from mother to child during breastfeed with appropriate medical interventions;
(b) if so, the details of steps being taken;
(c) whether Government is taking measures in collaborating with healthcare providers to facilitate linkage of HIV infected women to their nearest public health center and ensure that all HIV-infected pregnant women receive the treatment promptly; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether a farmer needs a big amount to install a solar plant up to two megawatts under PM-Kusum Component 'A' scheme of the Ministry;
(b) whether the cost of a one megawatt plant is ?5 crore and 70 percent of this amount has to be availed as a loan from the bank and whether this is not being made available to the farmers by the bank; and
(c) in such a situation whether Government would direct the banks to provide loans to farmers for a long period to provide relief to farmers and for success of the scheme?

(a) whether it is a fact that Bharat Sanchar Nigam Limited (BSNL), a very important institution of the Government, is heavily debt-ridden while private companies are making profits;
(b) whether Government has formulated any plan to strengthen BSNL and make it debt-free;
(c) if so, the detailed description of the said plan along with the time by when BSNL would become debt-free; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?
J

(a) whether Government has taken any strict stand towards tightening the safety standards and preventing negligence to avert the increasing incidents of fire in multi-storey buildings in the country, if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor;
(b) whether the Central Government proposes to provide assistance to the States to expand and modernize the fire services across the country;
(c) if so, the details thereof, State-wise; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?
J

(a) whether Government is considering the establishment of a new food park in Jharkhand, given the only sanctioned Mega Food Park for Jharkhand was canceled in 2019 due to unsatisfactory progress;
(b) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor;
(c) the details of the number of projects approved, completed and under progress in Jharkhand under the Pradhan Mantri Formalization of Micro Food Processing Enterprise (PMFME) Scheme; and
(d) the details of the funds sanctioned and released in FY 23-24 under PMFME Scheme for the State of Jharkhand?
J

(a) the steps taken by Government to boost the tourism sector in Ladakh;
(b) whether Government has made plans to make all the forbidden zones accessible to tourists in Ladakh;
(c) if so, details of the steps taken to ensure the safety and security of the tourists in these forbidden areas; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has provided any humanitarian assistance to the affected population in Ukraine due to the ongoing conflict with Russia; 
(b) the details of steps taken by Government to address the humanitarian crisis resulting from the conflict, particularly in terms of providing aid and support to affected communities; 
(c) whether Government has plans to further extend assistance to ensure the well-being and safety of civilians affected by the conflict; and
(d) if so, details thereof?

(a) whether Government plans to introduce any training program for the Anganwadi workers to make PM Poshan Tracker effective;
(b) if so, the details thereof, if not, the reasons therefor;
(c) whether Government is cognizant about the fact that the tech available for the use of Poshan Tracker is mostly non-functional in the States of Maharashtra and Andhra Pradesh; 
(d) if so, whether Government is planning to take any measures to replace the non-functional tech, if not, the reasons therefor; and
(e) whether Government has set up a timeline for the replacement of the non-functional tech?
BS

(a) whether any evaluation has been conducted at pan India level to take stock of teacher to student ratio in tribal districts;
(b) if so, the details of its key findings with special emphasis on the State of Jharkhand;
(c) whether Government aware of unique culture of tribal community across India; and 
(d) if so, how recruited teachers in the schools dedicatedly established for tribal communities and in every school established by Government in tribal districts are trained and evaluated on their sensitivity and understanding of tribal customs?

(a) whether Government has any exclusive health insurance schemes for Particularly Vulnerable Tribal Groups (PVTGs), taking into account of the large population of PVGTs from the States of Jharkhand, Maharashtra, etc;
(b) if so, the details thereof, and if not, the reasons therefor;
(c) whether Government has included the PVTGs in the Ayushman Bharat Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY);
(d) if so, the number of people from PVTGs who have availed AB-PMJAY services from Jharkhand since the inception of the AB-PMJAY scheme; and
(e) if not, how the new Pradhan Mantri Janjati Adivasi Nyaya Maha Abhiyan (PM JANMAN) will be ensuring health insurance benefits for PVTGs?

(a) whether it is a fact that the number of crimes occurring in railway station premises has risen by 105 per cent in 2023 as compared to 2021;
(b) if so, the details of actions initiated by Government to curb the rise in crimes at railway stations across the country;
(c) whether the railway stations face shortage in deployment of Railway Protection Force (RPF) which is a leading cause in rise in crimes; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and the measures initiated to address the shortage in deployment of RPF staff in railway stations and their premises?

(a) whether it is a fact that a large number of farmers are excluded from Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi Yojana (PM-KISAN) due to changes in digital framework of the scheme, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government has taken any initiative to reinstate such farmers into the scheme, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the details of cities and villages identified in the State of Jharkhand under the National Clean Air Programme to prevent, control and reduce air pollution;
(b) the details of targets fixed for those cities and villages;
(c) the roadmap to achieve the targets;
(d) by when the targets are likely to be achieved; and
(e) whether the 15th Finance Commission has recommended performance based grants for cities and villages in Jharkhand, if so, the relevant details thereof?

(a)the details of the policy of Government to ensure balanced development of all villages through Panchayati Raj Institutions (PRIs) in the country and the details of villages in Ranchi which will be benefited from it;
(b) the details of the amount allocated to the Panchayats of State of Jharkhand during the last four years and the current year; and
(c) the details of the amount allocated to the Panchayats of Uttar Pradesh, West Bengal, Rajasthan, Karnataka and Gujarat during the last four years?

(a) whether the expansion project of Tenughat Vidyut Nigam Limited is not a pressing necessity, in view of the increasing energy demand in the State of Jharkhand, at present;
(b) the reason for the delay in granting approval to TOR for 2×660 MW under its expansion project despite availability of suitable land, water, allotted coal block and some infrastructure etc. with Tenughat Vidyut Nigam Limited for expansion, the reason for its pendency; and 
(c) by when it is likely to be approved?

(a) whether it is a fact that the case related to approval for Jharkhand Horticulture Institute situated at Dumka Airport in Jharkhand is pending with the DGCA;
(b) if so, by when the approval for this will be given by the DGCA; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether the dissolution of the Dhalbhumgarh Airport in East Singhbhum, Jharkhand has been approved by the Airports Authority of India;
(b) if so, the reason therefor; and
(c) if not, by when Government proposes to start operations of Dhalbhumgarh Airport?

(a) whether ?44.60 crore was sanctioned in Trade Infrastructure for Export Scheme (TIES) meeting held in 2019 for the construction of the World Trade Centre in Ranchi;
(b) whether after disbursal of first installment the project has been cancelled and demand has been made to return the sanctioned amount with interest;
(c) whether the State Government's request for reconsideration was rejected;
(d) whether the establishment of the World Trade Centre in Ranchi would increase the possibilities of export of products immensely and play an important role in the progressive development of the State; and
(e) whether Government proposes to reapprove this scheme?

(a) the number of installments of the total due amount of the GST collection share as released to the State of Jharkhand for the Financial Year 2022-2023;
(b) whether any amount of GST share payable to the State of Jharkhand for the previous financial year is pending, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the total number of installments of GST payable to the State of Jharkhand released during this financial year; and
(d) whether there is any possibility of the States, especially Jharkhand, getting a higher share in view of the better collection of GST this year and whether the funds will be distributed accordingly?
J

(a) whether Government has taken any effective measures to extinguish the underground fire burning for a long time in the Jharia coalfields of Jharkhand in the last five years;
(b) if so, the extent of success achieved in extinguishing the fire;
(c) if not, the reasons therefor; and
(d) whether Government will assign the responsibility of dealing with this critical situation to the National Disaster Management Authority to save burning of approximately two billion tons of precious coking coal, to protect lives and properties of local residents as well as protect the environment by considering this a national disaster?

(a) whether Government is taking any concrete steps to reduce the unexpected increase in domestic air fares in airlines operated by private companies of the country on special occasions;
(b) if so, the details thereof; and
